  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser or run `vite build` here, so I haven't seen a rendered frame. The lighting values and the camera framing are untested.\n\nThe robot is built from primitives (capsules, spheres, boxes) in a nested group hierarchy, with no model files. Its joints are the neck/head, chest, two shoulders, two elbows, two hips and two knees.\n\nThe idle animation runs in `app.onFrame`. It has these parts:\n- **Breathing:** the hips bob slightly and the chest tilts with a sine wave.\n- **Weight shift:** a slow side-to-side sway moves the hips and alternately bends the knees.\n- **Head and arms:** the head turns and tilts, and the shoulders and elbows drift gently.\n\nLighting is a strong warm key light that casts the shadow on a grey floor, plus magenta and cyan rim lights from behind and a near-black background. The environment light is kept low.\n\nThe camera is a fixed perspective camera on the centre line, aimed at the robot's midpoint (about y = 1).\n\n`window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true after the first frame is drawn.\n\nI adapted the layout and animation from the repo's procedural humanoid recipe.",
